  "caveat": "Integrated Gradients satisfies completeness/sensitivity axioms, giving a stronger causal-adjacent attribution than raw attention (../simple_interpretability/). It still only explains the TRAINED MODEL's learned function, not ground-truth clinical causality between diagnoses. Raw positive-attribution mass by category is confounded by each category's overall base rate among input codes (the most frequent input categories -- CIR, END, DIG, MBD, GEN -- dominated every label's raw ranking before this was corrected); category_attribution_lift divides by category_baseline_share to control for this, analogous to eda/09's cooccur-rate/baseline-rate lift. Comparisons against eda/09 use the lift-ranked categories. Baseline = all-PAD word embedding; age/segment/position embeddings held at their real values so only each code's identity is attributed."
}